L380,994L383,995L382,1000L386,1005L386,1009L389,1019L402,1026L403,1029L402,1030L400,1031L389,1027L385,1027L383,1029L383,1032L380,1035L377,1033L382,1019L379,1013L375,1010L376,1009L374,1005L362,990L352,991L351,992L349,995L348,995L347,993L347,989L347,987L354,982L354,977L347,969L334,971L334,969L337,963L336,959L325,951L333,945L340,949L344,948L346,945L344,937L337,931L337,930L337,926L342,922L343,913L338,909L329,907L330,903L336,900L338,896L337,893L340,885L338,880L334,879L324,883L321,881L320,879L321,876L326,862L325,861L322,865L320,865L314,858L312,859L308,863L307,867L302,863L296,866L294,869L286,857L286,855L293,855L296,853L297,850L291,848L289,845L296,842L299,839L300,833L297,829L295,828L290,829L286,827L280,828L280,827L281,824L290,817L289,816L283,813L279,815L274,810L271,810L269,810L269,811L271,818L269,819L267,822L263,824L259,824L257,819L257,811L255,805L252,800L247,797L241,796L238,794L234,792L232,790L227,777L222,775L214,766L208,764L203,759L198,756L197,756L197,761L203,783L210,787L215,793L223,791L223,801L227,805L233,806L233,809L234,811L240,815L239,823L243,831L246,833L252,832L249,840L250,844L258,851L253,852L244,848L238,858L234,857L237,843L236,839L233,835L229,833L223,834L218,837L215,837L219,833L221,827L220,820L214,811L208,805L201,803L198,804L196,807L196,810L193,821L187,827L185,826L182,821L183,815L178,809L178,805L179,800L178,798L175,796L174,794L176,786L176,783L170,777L174,773L175,770L170,763L172,756L171,752L167,748L166,744L168,739L168,730L166,725L159,723L151,724L142,719L143,716L138,712L135,711L130,713L123,714L118,710L92,706L84,700L81,700L75,708L74,728L62,728L61,721L62,719L60,715L51,716L48,714L51,691L49,673L44,654L37,640ZM814,359L816,359L819,364L824,367L831,364L833,360L828,357L811,354L814,359Z","places":[["Carters Dam",63,674,"start"],["Worley Creek",401,304,"start"],["Camp Branch",675,1053,"start"],["Coosawattee River",866,30,"end"]],"km":150.21},"periods":{"winter":{"stripers":{"doing":"Stripers follow bait into the middle and backs of creeks. On calm, cloudy mornings they roll on top; after a cold front they drop deeper and need live bait.","how":[["Find them","Gulls and loons over the water, then bait on the graph."],["On top","Lead-head fluke, bucktail or small jerkbait cast to rolling fish."],["Live bait","Blueback herring or trout on freelines, or downlines when fish are deep."],["After a front","Downlines or a four-arm umbrella rig trolled slowly."]],"bands":[[0,8,"Rolling on top","in creeks"],[20,40,"Downlines","after fronts"]],"src":"t"},"spots":{"doing":"Spotted bass group up deep on ditches, channel swings, roadbeds and bluffs, often 25 to 45 ft, and move little.","how":[["Deep","Drop shot, jigging spoon or blade bait on the fish you mark."],["Bluffs and rock","Jerkbait or football jig, slowly."],["Early","Some school in shallow ditch backs at first light; slow-roll an underspin."]],"bands":[[25,45,"Ditches and","channels"]],"src":"t"},"walleye":{"doing":"Walleye stage toward the river and creek backs in late winter ahead of a night spawn.","how":[["Night","Floating minnow plugs or shallow crankbaits on riprap and creek backs."],["Day","Jig and minnow slowly near the river channel."]],"bands":[[0,10,"Riprap and","creek backs"],[20,35,"River channel"]],"src":"t"}},"prespawn":{"stripers":{"doing":"Live shad or alewives on downlines about 50 ft. Early, fish shallow creeks like Worley and the Beach with boards. At night, artificials on points and markers in under 25 ft.","how":[["Downlines","Shad or alewives at about 50 ft."],["Boards","Slightly weighted lines about 50 ft back, early in the creeks."],["U-rigs","About 3 mph, 150 ft back; vary speed and distance."],["Night","Artificials on points and shallow markers."]],"bands":[[0,25,"Creeks early,","points at night"],[45,55,"Downlines"]],"src":"r"},"spots":{"doing":"About 75 percent of fish are shallow through the day on transition banks that get the most sun, especially where deep turns shallow or rock turns to clay. Warm nights and sun matter more than the high.","how":[["Lures","Crankbait, jerkbait, shaky head."]],"bands":[[2,12,"Sunny transition","banks"]],"src":"r"},"walleye":{"doing":"Shallow: the backs of creeks, riprap on the dam and the river. They spawn at night, so feed right before dawn or at dusk. Mostly males.","how":[["Lures","Original floating Rapala, DT6 and DT10, slow small shad imitations."],["Jig","1/4 oz jig and minnow, slowly and thoroughly."]],"bands":[[0,10,"Shallow at","night"]],"src":"r"}},"spawn":{"stripers":{"doing":"Herring stage up the creeks and stripers school on top for the first couple of hours of light, then settle to 25 to 35 ft in the same areas.","how":[["First light","Topwater and freelined bluebacks over the herring."],["After the sun is up","Downline bluebacks at 25 to 35 ft nearby."],["Clouds","A cloudy morning can keep the topwater bite going to mid-morning."]],"bands":[[0,6,"Topwater","at dawn"],[25,35,"Downlines","mid-day"]],"src":"t"},"spots":{"doing":"Largemouth bed in pockets in the 60s; spotted bass bed deeper, often 10 to 15 ft, on gravel and flat rock. The full moon pushes waves of fish up.","how":[["Beds","Shaky head, wacky rig or Fluke around beds and the bank between them."],["Points","Jerkbait across the points into spawning coves."]],"bands":[[2,15,"Beds; spots","deeper"]],"src":"t"},"walleye":{"doing":"Post-spawn walleye drift back toward points and the main lake.","how":[["Points","Jig and minnow or crankbait at dawn and dusk."]],"bands":[[8,20,"Points"]],"src":"t"}},"latespring":{"stripers":{"doing":"The herring spawn on points, clay banks, riprap and marina walls at first light, and stripers crash them. By June they slide to brush on points in 15 to 35 ft, then deeper.","how":[["Dawn","Walking bait, popper or wake bait on points and humps."],["Live bait","Herring pitched or freelined to points."],["Later","Downlines over brush in 15 to 35 ft."]],"bands":[[0,6,"Topwater","at dawn"],[15,35,"Brush on","points"]],"src":"t"},"spots":{"doing":"Bass key on the herring and shad spawn on hard banks at dawn, then move to brush on points and humps as the water heads into the 80s.","how":[["Dawn","Topwater or wake bait on clay points, bridges and marina walls."],["Parallel","Underspin, white spinnerbait or Fluke run along walls and riprap."],["Later","Drop shot or shaky head on brush in 15 to 25 ft."]],"bands":[[0,6,"Bait spawn","at dawn"],[15,25,"Brush"]],"src":"t"},"walleye":{"doing":"Walleye feed on herring around points and humps at low light.","how":[["Low light","Crankbaits and live herring on points."]],"bands":[[10,25,"Points and","humps"]],"src":"t"}},"summer":{"stripers":{"doing":"35 to 50 ft early by the beach and marina; hybrids at the mouths of Worley Creek and Camp Branch. Umbrella rigs later in the day, especially in stained water.","how":[["Early","Live bait at 35 to 50 ft."],["Later","Captain Mack umbrella rig 150 ft back."]],"bands":[[35,50,"Early, near","the marina"]],"src":"r"},"spots":{"doing":"25 to 35 ft, suspended off main-lake points and sharp drop-offs. A short early topwater bite on busting spots.","how":[["Early","Topwater to busting fish; it fades fast."],["Then","Drop shot or jig on the suspended fish."]],"bands":[[0,4,"Busting early"],[25,35,"Off points"]],"src":"r"},"walleye":{"doing":"Deep offshore structure with baitfish, especially when the dam is generating. They stay deep until turnover.","how":[["Live bait","Fresh herring; light leaders and small hooks."],["Lights","Catch bait under Hydroglow lights."],["When","Early, late or at night."]],"bands":[[30,50,"Offshore","structure"]],"src":"r"}},"fall":{"stripers":{"doing":"As the water cools, schools rise out of the depths and blow up on points and humps. Turnover kills the bite in creeks that have turned, so fish the clear water.","how":[["Blowups","Run to surface schools and come in upwind."],["Lures","Walking baits in calm water, swimbaits or a Magic Swimmer in wind; a spoon under marked fish."],["Live bait","Herring freelined about 100 ft back over humps and points."],["Wind or traffic","Umbrella rigs at 2.5 to 3.5 mph."]],"bands":[[0,8,"Schools","on top"],[10,30,"Spoon under","marked fish"]],"src":"t"},"spots":{"doing":"As the thermocline breaks, spots school with shad on points and humps, and some follow bait into creek ditches. Turned-over water is dead water.","how":[["Schools","Swimbaits and topwater on humps and points."],["Wind","Spinnerbait or crankbait on windy rock and clay banks."],["Deep","Spoon or drop shot in 25 to 50 ft ditches."]],"bands":[[0,15,"Schooling","and wind"],[25,45,"Ditches"]],"src":"t"},"walleye":{"doing":"Walleye stay deep until turnover, then move up onto points.","how":[["Points","Jig and minnow or trolled crankbaits."]],"bands":[[15,35,"Points"]],"src":"t"}}},"zones":[{"sp":"stripers","p":["prespawn","spawn","winter"],"name":"Worley Creek","t":"Early boards in the creek.","src":"r","c":[[387,304,55],[316,228,45]]},{"sp":"stripers","p":["latespring","summer"],"name":"Beach and marina area","t":"35 to 50 ft early.","src":"r","c":[[560,900,70]]},{"sp":"stripers","p":["latespring","summer","fall"],"name":"Mouths of Worley Creek and Camp Branch","t":"Hybrids at the creek mouths.","src":"r","c":[[470,445,60],[640,930,55]]},{"sp":"stripers","p":["fall"],"name":"Main lake near the dam","t":"Schools as the water cools.","src":"t","c":[[200,700,70]]},{"sp":"spots","p":["winter","prespawn","spawn","latespring","summer","fall"],"name":"Main-lake points","t":"Sunny transition banks in spring; suspended off points in summer.","src":"r","c":[[300,600,60],[600,600,60],[450,800,55]]},{"sp":"walleye","p":["winter","prespawn","spawn"],"name":"Dam riprap","t":"Night walleye on the riprap.","src":"r","c":[[57,673,50]]},{"sp":"walleye","p":["winter","prespawn","spawn"],"name":"Creek backs and the river","t":"Shallow at night before the spawn.","src":"r","c":[[880,80,50],[820,602,40],[762,884,40]]},{"sp":"walleye","p":["latespring","summer","fall"],"name":"Deep offshore structure","t":"Deep main lake with bait.","src":"t","c":[[350,750,70],[600,700,60]]}],"sources":[["GON Carters report, Mar 2025","https://gon.com/?p=1122286"],["GON Carters report, Aug 2022","https://gon.com/?p=877155"]]}